WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.162
The next night the four children and Mademoiselle walked across the castle lawn.

2
00:00:08.163 --> 00:00:11.019
The moon had not yet risen.

3
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:18.889
They walked until they reached a hilltop where there was a circle of huge stones.

4
00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:23.212
One had an odd-looking hole near the top.

5
00:00:23.213 --> 00:00:28.388
"This must be the Temple of Strange Stones," thought Gerald.

6
00:00:28.389 --> 00:00:34.893
Lord Yalding was already sitting there.

7
00:00:34.894 --> 00:00:40.843
He told Mademoiselle to leave.

8
00:00:40.844 --> 00:00:47.273
"Never!" she cried, kneeling next to him.

9
00:00:47.274 --> 00:00:50.137
"If you are mad, then I am mad too.

10
00:00:50.138 --> 00:00:52.373
I believe the children's tales.

11
00:00:52.374 --> 00:00:57.111
I'm here to see whatever the rising moon will show us."

12
00:00:57.112 --> 00:01:02.414
Lord Yalding put the ring on her finger, and they stood together.

13
00:01:02.415 --> 00:01:06.672
A faint grayness touched the top of the rock with the hole.

14
00:01:06.673 --> 00:01:14.229
Then the hole was a disk of light as a moonbeam shone through it.

15
00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:18.464
Suddenly a fountain of light was released.

16
00:01:18.465 --> 00:01:25.319
All sorts of statues—dinosaurs, dragons, angels—began to approach the circle.

17
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.098
Last of all came the gods and goddesses from the island.

18
00:01:29.099 --> 00:01:36.047
Each stone statue came quietly into the circle of light.

19
00:01:36.048 --> 00:01:41.714
Hermes had told the children to ask about the magic at the Temple of Strange Stones.

20
00:01:41.715 --> 00:01:44.459
But no one said a word.

21
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:49.537
The light started to move away.

22
00:01:49.538 --> 00:01:57.028
"I want to go to the passage on the island," Mademoiselle said suddenly.

23
00:01:57.029 --> 00:02:03.132
The two adults and the children rowed to the island and found the steps.

24
00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:09.870
Guided by candles they walked through the darkness toward the glowing statue of Psyche.

25
00:02:09.871 --> 00:02:14.615
They were in the Hall of Granted Wishes.

26
00:02:14.616 --> 00:02:21.447
"I realized something at the Temple of Strange Stones," Mademoiselle explained to Lord Yalding.

27
00:02:21.448 --> 00:02:25.489
"The ring is the magic ring given long ago to a mortal.

28
00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:31.774
It was given to your ancestor by one of my ancestors.

29
00:02:31.775 --> 00:02:34.481
She wanted him to build her a house.

30
00:02:34.482 --> 00:02:39.895
So this place was built partly by his love and partly by magic.

31
00:02:39.896 --> 00:02:42.501
But she never lived to see it.

32
00:02:42.502 --> 00:02:48.040
That was the price of the magic."

33
00:02:48.041 --> 00:02:51.641
"The price?" asked Lord Yalding.

34
00:02:51.642 --> 00:02:58.613
"Whenever you use the ring, it requires a payment," said Mademoiselle.

35
00:02:58.614 --> 00:03:03.767
"Your price for wishing for me to appear was to go mad."

36
00:03:03.768 --> 00:03:07.628
"What's our payment?" asked Gerald.

37
00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:11.688
"Children don't have to pay," said Mademoiselle.

38
00:03:11.689 --> 00:03:17.015
"For us adults only one wish is free, and that is the last wish.

39
00:03:17.016 --> 00:03:19.245
Shall I wish it?"

40
00:03:19.246 --> 00:03:22.931
"Yes!" they all said.

41
00:03:22.932 --> 00:03:28.851
"I wish that all the magic done by this ring will be undone."

42
00:03:28.852 --> 00:03:32.508
She turned to Lord Yalding.

43
00:03:32.509 --> 00:03:39.019
"And that this ring will be just a charm that binds us together."

44
00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:44.774
The enchanted light surrounding Psyche instantly went out.

45
00:03:44.775 --> 00:03:51.092
The scenes of granted wishes went dark.

46
00:03:51.093 --> 00:03:54.386
Then Psyche's statue disappeared.

47
00:03:54.387 --> 00:03:59.076
In its place was a stone.

48
00:03:59.077 --> 00:04:04.817
"It is my ancestor's grave," said Mademoiselle.

49
00:04:04.818 --> 00:04:09.118
They returned to the castle.

50
00:04:09.119 --> 00:04:20.245
The next day Mademoiselle awoke and found a plain gold ring clasped in her hand.

51
00:04:20.246 --> 00:04:24.458
More than half the jewels in the treasure room were gone.

52
00:04:24.459 --> 00:04:28.474
Large pieces of the castle itself were missing.

53
00:04:28.475 --> 00:04:35.078
The children realized that Lord Yalding's ancestor had used the ring to help him build it.

54
00:04:35.079 --> 00:04:40.208
But there were enough jewels left to pay for anything Lord Yalding wanted.

55
00:04:40.209 --> 00:04:45.791
And what he wanted was to marry Mademoiselle.

56
00:04:45.792 --> 00:04:49.451
By the end of the summer, he had his wish.

57
00:04:49.452 --> 00:04:56.733
The ring was slipped onto Mademoiselle's finger and she became Lady Yalding.

58
00:04:56.734 --> 00:05:00.967
They lived happily ever after.

59
00:05:00.968 --> 00:05:14.336
And each year during the holidays, their young friends visited them at the castle.

